{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Table is a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Headless UI"}]},{"type":"text","value":" library for building powerful tables & datagrids for TS/JS, React, Vue, Solid, Qwik, and Svelte."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-is-headless-ui","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What is \"headless\" UI?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Headless UI"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is a term for libraries and utilities that provide the logic, state, processing and API for UI elements and interactions, but "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"do not provide markup, styles, or pre-built implementations"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Scratching your head yet? 😉 Headless UI has a few main goals:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hardest parts of building complex UIs usually revolve around state, events, side-effects, data computation/management. By removing these concerns from the markup, styles and implementation details, our logic and components can be more modular and reusable."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Building UI is a very branded and custom experience, even if that means choosing a design system or adhering to a design spec. To support this custom experience, component-based UI libraries need to support a massive (and seemingly endless) API surface around markup and style customization. Headless UI libraries decouple your logic from your UI"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you use a headless UI library, the complex task of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"data-processing, state-management, and business logic"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are handled for you, leaving you to worry about higher-cardinality decisions that differ across implementations and use cases."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Want to dive deeper? "},{"type":"link","href":"https://www.merrickchristensen.com/articles/headless-user-interface-components/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read more about Headless UI"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"component-based-libraries-vs-headless-libraries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component-based libraries vs Headless libraries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the ecosystem of table/datagrid libraries, there are two main categories:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component-based table libraries"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Headless table libraries"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"which-kind-of-table-library-should-i-use","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which kind of table library should I use?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each approach has subtle tradeoffs. Understanding these subtleties will help you make the right decision for your application and team."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"component-based-table-libraries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component-based Table Libraries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component-based table libraries will typically supply you with a feature-rich drop-in solution and ready-to-use components/markup complete with styles/theming. "},{"type":"link","href":"https://ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/?utm_source=reacttable&utm_campaign=githubreacttable","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AG Grid"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is a great example of this type of table library."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pros:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ship with ready-to-use markup/styles"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Little setup required"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Turn-key experience"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cons:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Less control over markup"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom styles are typically theme-based"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Larger bundle-sizes"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Highly coupled to framework adapters and platforms"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want a ready-to-use table and design/bundle-size are not hard requirements"}]},{"type":"text","value":", then you should consider using a component-based table library."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are a lot of component-based table libraries out there, but we believe "},{"type":"link","href":"https://ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/?utm_source=reacttable&utm_campaign=githubreacttable","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AG Grid"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is the gold standard and is by far our favorite grid-sibling (don't tell the others 🤫)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"headless-table-libraries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Headless Table Libraries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Headless table libraries will typically supply you with functions, state, utilities and event listeners to build your own table markup or attach to existing table markups."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pros:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full control over markup and styles"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supports all styling patterns (CSS, CSS-in-JS, UI libraries, etc)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Smaller bundle-sizes"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Portable. Run anywhere JS runs!"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cons:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"More setup required"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No markup, styles or themes provided"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want a lighter-weight table or full control over the design"}]},{"type":"text","value":", then you should consider using a headless table library."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are very few headless table libraries out there and obviously, "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Table"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is our favorite!"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"what-is-headless-ui","text":"What is \"headless\" UI?","level":2},{"id":"component-based-libraries-vs-headless-libraries","text":"Component-based libraries vs Headless libraries","level":2},{"id":"which-kind-of-table-library-should-i-use","text":"Which kind of table library should I use?","level":3},{"id":"component-based-table-libraries","text":"Component-based Table Libraries","level":3},{"id":"headless-table-libraries","text":"Headless Table Libraries","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Table is a **Headless UI** library for building powerful tables & datagrids for TS/JS, React, Vue, Solid, Qwik, and Svelte.\n\n## What is \"headless\" UI?\n\n**Headless UI** is a term for libraries and utilities that provide the logic, state, processing and API for UI elements and interactions, but **do not provide markup, styles, or pre-built implementations**. Scratching your head yet? 😉 Headless UI has a few main goals:\n\nThe hardest parts of building complex UIs usually revolve around state, events, side-effects, data computation/management. By removing these concerns from the markup, styles and implementation details, our logic and components can be more modular and reusable.\n\nBuilding UI is a very branded and custom experience, even if that means choosing a design system or adhering to a design spec. To support this custom experience, component-based UI libraries need to support a massive (and seemingly endless) API surface around markup and style customization. Headless UI libraries decouple your logic from your UI\n\nWhen you use a headless UI library, the complex task of **data-processing, state-management, and business logic** are handled for you, leaving you to worry about higher-cardinality decisions that differ across implementations and use cases.\n\n> Want to dive deeper? [Read more about Headless UI](https://www.merrickchristensen.com/articles/headless-user-interface-components/).\n\n## Component-based libraries vs Headless libraries\n\nIn the ecosystem of table/datagrid libraries, there are two main categories:\n\n- Component-based table libraries\n- Headless table libraries\n\n### Which kind of table library should I use?\n\nEach approach has subtle tradeoffs. Understanding these subtleties will help you make the right decision for your application and team.\n\n### Component-based Table Libraries\n\nComponent-based table libraries will typically supply you with a feature-rich drop-in solution and ready-to-use components/markup complete with styles/theming. [AG Grid](https://ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/?utm_source=reacttable&utm_campaign=githubreacttable) is a great example of this type of table library.\n\n**Pros:**\n\n- Ship with ready-to-use markup/styles\n- Little setup required\n- Turn-key experience\n\n**Cons:**\n\n- Less control over markup\n- Custom styles are typically theme-based\n- Larger bundle-sizes\n- Highly coupled to framework adapters and platforms\n\n**If you want a ready-to-use table and design/bundle-size are not hard requirements**, then you should consider using a component-based table library.\n\nThere are a lot of component-based table libraries out there, but we believe [AG Grid](https://ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/?utm_source=reacttable&utm_campaign=githubreacttable) is the gold standard and is by far our favorite grid-sibling (don't tell the others 🤫).\n\n### Headless Table Libraries\n\nHeadless table libraries will typically supply you with functions, state, utilities and event listeners to build your own table markup or attach to existing table markups.\n\n**Pros:**\n\n- Full control over markup and styles\n- Supports all styling patterns (CSS, CSS-in-JS, UI libraries, etc)\n- Smaller bundle-sizes\n- Portable. Run anywhere JS runs!\n\n**Cons:**\n\n- More setup required\n- No markup, styles or themes provided\n\n**If you want a lighter-weight table or full control over the design**, then you should consider using a headless table library.\n\nThere are very few headless table libraries out there and obviously, **TanStack Table** is our favorite!\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Introduction\n---\n\nTanStack Table is a **Headless UI** library for building powerful tables & datagrids for TS/JS, React, Vue, Solid, Qwik, and Svelte.\n\n## What is \"headless\" UI?\n\n**Headless UI** is a term for libraries and utilities that provide the logic, state, processing and API for UI elements and interactions, but **do not provide markup, styles, or pre-built implementations**. Scratching your head yet? 😉 Headless UI has a few main goals:\n\nThe hardest parts of building complex UIs usually revolve around state, events, side-effects, data computation/management. By removing these concerns from the markup, styles and implementation details, our logic and components can be more modular and reusable.\n\nBuilding UI is a very branded and custom experience, even if that means choosing a design system or adhering to a design spec. To support this custom experience, component-based UI libraries need to support a massive (and seemingly endless) API surface around markup and style customization. Headless UI libraries decouple your logic from your UI\n\nWhen you use a headless UI library, the complex task of **data-processing, state-management, and business logic** are handled for you, leaving you to worry about higher-cardinality decisions that differ across implementations and use cases.\n\n> Want to dive deeper? [Read more about Headless UI](https://www.merrickchristensen.com/articles/headless-user-interface-components/).\n\n## Component-based libraries vs Headless libraries\n\nIn the ecosystem of table/datagrid libraries, there are two main categories:\n\n- Component-based table libraries\n- Headless table libraries\n\n### Which kind of table library should I use?\n\nEach approach has subtle tradeoffs. Understanding these subtleties will help you make the right decision for your application and team.\n\n### Component-based Table Libraries\n\nComponent-based table libraries will typically supply you with a feature-rich drop-in solution and ready-to-use components/markup complete with styles/theming. [AG Grid](https://ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/?utm_source=reacttable&utm_campaign=githubreacttable) is a great example of this type of table library.\n\n**Pros:**\n\n- Ship with ready-to-use markup/styles\n- Little setup required\n- Turn-key experience\n\n**Cons:**\n\n- Less control over markup\n- Custom styles are typically theme-based\n- Larger bundle-sizes\n- Highly coupled to framework adapters and platforms\n\n**If you want a ready-to-use table and design/bundle-size are not hard requirements**, then you should consider using a component-based table library.\n\nThere are a lot of component-based table libraries out there, but we believe [AG Grid](https://ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/?utm_source=reacttable&utm_campaign=githubreacttable) is the gold standard and is by far our favorite grid-sibling (don't tell the others 🤫).\n\n### Headless Table Libraries\n\nHeadless table libraries will typically supply you with functions, state, utilities and event listeners to build your own table markup or attach to existing table markups.\n\n**Pros:**\n\n- Full control over markup and styles\n- Supports all styling patterns (CSS, CSS-in-JS, UI libraries, etc)\n- Smaller bundle-sizes\n- Portable. Run anywhere JS runs!\n\n**Cons:**\n\n- More setup required\n- No markup, styles or themes provided\n\n**If you want a lighter-weight table or full control over the design**, then you should consider using a headless table library.\n\nThere are very few headless table libraries out there and obviously, **TanStack Table** is our favorite!\n"}
